  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fix KlapTransport not honoring DeviceConfiguration.Timeout on .NET 10: the non-net472 HttpClient-based request path (used for handshake and encrypted requests) only respected whatever CancellationToken the caller supplied and never derived a deadline from the configured Timeout, unlike the net472 HttpWebRequest fallback and TpapTransport. A caller that did not supply its own deadline (e.g. CancellationToken.None) would silently fall back to the shared HttpClient's runtime default of about 100 seconds instead of the configured timeout. KlapTransport now wraps every non-net472 request with a per-call timeout derived from DeviceConfiguration.Timeout, matching the behavior already present in TpapTransport and the net472 KLAP fallback.",
